<title>USA: US aluminum service center shipments up in Jan-Jun.</title>
<headline>US aluminum service center shipments up in Jan-Jun.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. service center shipments of aluminum mill products for the first half of the year were 9.9 percent higher than shipments in last year's corresponding period, according to the National Association of Aluminum Distributors.</p>
<p>According to NAAD's three month moving average index, shipments in June rose to 105.9 points compared with 101.5 points in May and 94.2 points in June 1996. Inventory rose to 104.7 points in June from 103.8 points in May and 104.3 points in June 1996.</p>
<p>Distributors were carrying 2.7 months of inventory in June, compared with 2.8 months in May and 3.0 months in June 1996.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
